  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Velvet Showcase",
    "overview": "The site is a jeweller's display case. Pearl Ivory and Velvet Tray charcoal are the cloth the pieces rest on. Baikunthh Gold is the glint where light catches metal, so it marks focus and value rather than covering surfaces. Photography is the jewel: images sit on Display Cream, in square or 3:4 frames, with nothing laid over them except at the moment of interaction.\n\nDensity is calm and edited. Pages breathe in generous vertical bands (about 96px between sections on desktop), while groups inside them stay tight. Interfaces are hushed: square corners, hairline borders and small spaced capitals carry the brand, so loud colour, heavy shadow or decoration is never needed to say \"luxury\". Charcoal bands (the announcement bar, the rates ticker, the brand-story band, the footer) bracket the light pages and give the scroll a rhythm, like the dark velvet edges of a tray.\n\nThe buying path is primary wherever it appears. Price is set in the display serif and given real size. The primary action is the one deep-gold surface on screen. Trust facts (hallmarking, buyback, insured bridal shipping) sit close to the commitment, not in decoration.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Light ivory pages bracketed by charcoal bands; no dark mode.",
      "High-contrast serif for names, titles and prices; Inter for everything functional.",
      "Square everything: buttons, inputs, cards, images, chips.",
      "Gold as light, not paint: rules, focus, selected states and the single primary action.",
      "Flat at rest; soft gold-tinted lift only on hover and for floating layers."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Glint Rule",
        "body": "Baikunthh Gold appears as lines, outlines, icons and small marks. It fills a surface only in its deep form, and then only for the primary action or a selected state.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Readable Gold Rule",
        "body": "White text sits only on Deep Baikunthh Gold or darker. Never put white text on Baikunthh Gold, and never put Baikunthh Gold text on ivory at body size.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Engraved Name Rule",
        "body": "Names of pieces, prices and page titles are always set in the display serif. Interface words (buttons, labels, filters) are always set in Inter capitals. Don't swap them.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Kicker Rule",
        "body": "No small uppercase label above a heading. The heading carries itself; a gold rule beneath it is the only ornament.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Aligned Figures Rule",
        "body": "Totals, summaries and price breakdowns use tabular figures, so rupee amounts line up in a column.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-By-Default Rule",
        "body": "Nothing casts a shadow unless the pointer is on it or it floats above the page. A hover lift may rise by 1px; never more.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** put white text only on Deep Baikunthh Gold (#8C703B) or darker, and keep Baikunthh Gold (#C5A059) for rules, outlines, icons and focus.",
      "**Do** start every page with the shared page shell and container, and measure every sticky offset from `--header-h`.",
      "**Do** set piece names, prices and page titles in Cormorant Garamond, and interface labels in Inter uppercase at 0.2em tracking.",
      "**Do** keep corners square on every control and container; reserve circles for badges, dots and radio marks.",
      "**Do** use Quiet Ink (#6B7280) or darker for any text on ivory or white.",
      "**Do** give every icon-only control an accessible name and every input an enclosing label.",
      "**Do** use tabular figures in totals and price breakdowns."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** place white text on Baikunthh Gold (#C5A059) or Burnished Hover (#B38F4D); both fail contrast.",
      "**Don't** add a small uppercase kicker label above a heading.",
      "**Don't** nest a surface card inside another surface card.",
      "**Don't** add shadows to resting elements or use grey, hard-offset or coloured-halo shadows.",
      "**Don't** rely on hover alone for an action; touch and keyboard must reach it too.",
      "**Don't** use emoji in place of icons; use Lucide icons at a consistent stroke.",
      "**Don't** pad pages to viewport height; let short pages end where their content ends."
    ]
  }
}